    equations: [['h_t = f(W_x x_t + W_h h_(t−1) + b)', 'A simplified vanilla recurrent update; it must wait for h_(t−1).'], ['dense_attention_work ∝ S² · d_head · H', 'Doubling S approximately quadruples pairwise score work when other dimensions stay fixed.'], ['window_attention_work ≈ S · w · d_head · H', 'With fixed window width w much smaller than S, direct comparisons scale approximately linearly in S.']],
    design: 'Prefer a Transformer for broad parallel training and flexible content interactions when capacity permits. Consider recurrent or state-space architectures for bounded streaming state or severe memory limits, but validate quality on tasks requiring remote context. Hybrid architectures can mix local attention and recurrent memory.',
    implementation: 'RNN: for t in tokens: h=cell(x[t],h). Transformer: Q,K,V=project(X); scores=Q@K.T; scores=mask(scores); Y=softmax(scores)@V. Sliding attention restricts mask to nearby positions.',
    performance: 'Compare prefill time, sequential critical path, training throughput, cache bytes, peak VRAM and accuracy by context distance. A fused attention implementation avoids the naive full attention matrix allocation; computational scaling for dense attention still matters.',
